`toContain` string scans over source text, and Mercury model-side AST evidence is explicitly disclaimed (HTTP 402). All structural claims rest on string matching and excerpt reading.\nINHERITED: run-empire-v2.js — `activeTf = (... ) || this.candleTimeframe` silent fallback default; `this.sessionRouter?.activeSession || 'unknown'` silent default in trace source labels; both unfixed. core/StateManager.js — `eventTimeMs = Date.now()` default parameter is an inherited trading-data default that lets time-omitting callers stamp wall-clock time, and `getLastPrice` returns `... || null` (falsy coercion pattern); both unfixed and unchanged, correctly so under the no-downstream-change ruling. CHANGELOG.md — none. test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js — string-scan test methodology inherited, unfixed.\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER: classified 3 of 3. (1) `canUpdateLastPrice` availability check — pre-existing guard restructured for trace reporting, not a new gate; true boundary (writer may legitimately be absent at wiring time). (2) StateManager monotonic rejection (`incomingTime < currentTime → false`) — unchanged true boundary, now a genuine staleness tripwire since units are canonical. (3) `ohlcTimestampMs` null-return on unparseable input flowing to a `false`/`mark_rejected` — producer-fixable ambiguity (invalid vs stale conflated in the trace label); no receipt shows it is unreachable.\nALLEGATIONS: (A) Probe/production function-identity gap (`toTimestampMs` vs `ohlcTimestampMs`) — SUBSTANTIVE, basis RECEIPT-absence (the run-empire-v2.js:923-990 receipt shows the name mismatch; no receipt closes it). (B) Un-enumerated `updateLastPrice` call sites undermine the minimum-repair totality claim — SUBSTANTIVE, TESTIMONY (EVIDENCE.md line-number assertions without excerpts). (C) `mark_rejected` conflates null-timestamp with stale frame — MECHANICAL, RECEIPT (StateManager.js:899-901 + ohlc-normalize.js null return). (D) Strategy isolation and trace honesty confirmed — no allegation; R